# 低频词汇 List07
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List07核心词汇

garrison /ˈɡærɪsn/ n./v. 驻军 The town had a small military garrison. 这个镇有一个小型驻军。
genocide /ˈdʒenəsaɪd/ n. 种族灭绝 The international community condemned the genocide. 国际社会谴责了种族灭绝。
glamour /ˈɡlæmə(r)/ n. 魅力 The glamour of Hollywood attracts many actors. 好莱坞的魅力吸引了很多演员。
glimpse /ɡlɪmps/ n./v. 一瞥 She caught a glimpse of the celebrity. 她瞥见了那位名人。
gratitude /ˈɡrætɪtjuːd/ n. 感激 He expressed his gratitude for the help. 他对帮助表示了感激。
grieve /ɡriːv/ v. 悲伤 The family grieved the loss of their loved one. 家人为失去亲人而悲伤。
grim /ɡrɪm/ adj. 严峻的 The economic outlook is grim. 经济前景严峻。
grudge /ɡrʌdʒ/ n./v. 怨恨 She holds a grudge against her former boss. 她对前老板怀有怨恨。
habitat /ˈhæbɪtæt/ n. 栖息地 The destruction of natural habitats threatens wildlife. 自然栖息地的破坏威胁着野生动物。
hail /heɪl/ v./n. 欢呼；冰雹 The discovery was hailed as a breakthrough. 这一发现被誉为一项突破。
hazard /ˈhæzəd/ n./v. 危险 Smoking is a health hazard. 吸烟是一种健康危害。
hemisphere /ˈhemɪsfɪə(r)/ n. 半球 Australia is in the Southern Hemisphere. 澳大利亚在南半球。
herald /ˈherəld/ v./n. 预示；先驱 The invention heralded a new era. 这项发明预示了一个新时代。
heritage /ˈherɪtɪdʒ/ n. 遗产 China has a rich cultural heritage. 中国有丰富的文化遗产。
hierarchy /ˈhaɪərɑːki/ n. 等级制度 The company has a strict hierarchy. 公司有严格的等级制度。
hospitable /hɒˈspɪtəbl/ adj. 好客的 The local people are very hospitable. 当地人非常好客。
hostage /ˈhɒstɪdʒ/ n. 人质 The hostages were released after negotiations. 人质在谈判后被释放。
hover /ˈhɒvə(r)/ v. 盘旋；徘徊 The helicopter hovered above the building. 直升机在建筑物上空盘旋。
humiliate /hjuːˈmilieɪt/ v. 羞辱 He felt humiliated by the public criticism. 公开批评让他感到羞辱。
hurdle /ˈhɜːdl/ n./v. 障碍；跨越 The biggest hurdle is lack of funding. 最大的障碍是缺乏资金。
hygiene /ˈhaɪdʒiːn/ n. 卫生 Good hygiene prevents the spread of disease. 良好的卫生习惯能防止疾病传播。
hypocritical /ˌhɪpəˈkrɪtɪkl/ adj. 虚伪的 It would be hypocritical to criticize others. 批评别人是虚伪的。
illicit /ɪˈlɪsɪt/ adj. 非法的 The police cracked down on illicit trade. 警方打击了非法贸易。
immerse /ɪˈmɜːs/ v. 沉浸 She immersed herself in the study of Chinese culture. 她沉浸在中国文化的研究中。
imminent /ˈɪmɪnənt/ adj. 迫在眉睫的 A major change is imminent. 重大变革迫在眉睫。
impair /ɪmˈpeə(r)/ v. 损害 Excessive drinking can impair liver function. 过量饮酒会损害肝功能。
impartial /ɪmˈpɑːʃəl/ adj. 公正的 The judge must be impartial. 法官必须公正。
impede /ɪmˈpiːd/ v. 阻碍 Bureaucracy can impede progress. 官僚主义会阻碍进步。
impetus /ˈɪmpɪtəs/ n. 推动力 The crisis provided the impetus for reform. 这场危机为改革提供了推动力。
imprison /ɪmˈprɪzn/ v. 监禁 He was imprisoned for five years. 他被监禁了五年。
